{
  "brief_rationale": "The trajectory met the discharge-transition responsibility chain: it repeatedly screened for neurologic/ocular/cardiac red flags, reconciled records and medication uncertainty, avoided self-directed anticoagulation, and converted follow-up into an executable ophthalmology plus cardiology/BP plan. It actively completed multiple high-order points, including tailored plain-language communication, adapting sequencing to family conflict/time constraints, synthesizing ECG/cardiology information without inventing atrial fibrillation, and revising the medication plan after cardiology prescribed antiplatelet/statin therapy. No serious or minor responsibility-chain error remains; the final plan was safe, executable, and confirmed by the caregiver, supporting grade 5.",
  "closure_assessment": {
    "citations": [
      {
        "event_id": "lite_evt_00329",
        "explanation": "Final doctor message confirms medication management, red flags, and follow-up are organized.",
        "quote": "你现在把药品管理、时间安排、风险识别和后续就诊都理得非常清楚"
      },
      {
        "event_id": "lite_evt_00343",
        "explanation": "Caregiver gives receipt that the medication plan and urgent thresholds are understood and actionable.",
        "quote": "我就不等了直接急诊"
      }
    ],
    "executable": true,
    "explanation": "Closure is bounded to the current discharge episode: medications are reconciled to prescription/pharmacy labels, eye follow-up is preserved, cardiovascular evaluation has occurred, BP and bleeding/stroke/cardiac red flags are specified, and the caregiver confirms execution.",
    "label": "valid_closure",
    "safe": true,
    "traceable": true
  },
